# The de Havilland Mosquito FB Mk VI's checklists: this project's own words,
# following the aeroplane's own Pilot's Notes.
#
# **The source is A.P. 2019E-P.N., January 1950, 2nd edition**, the same
# Pilot's Notes docs/ASSETS.md already records for this aircraft's figures and
# cites as [PN50]. Its own "PILOT'S CHECK LIST" runs to 128 numbered items on
# pages 6 to 10, and Part II gives the handling that goes with them. What is
# below is those drills in this project's own words, cut down to what a
# simulated aeroplane can be seen to do: the Notes' external walk-round, its
# dinghy, crash axe and first-aid kit, its intercom and its bomb doors have
# nothing here that could show them done.
#
# The item or paragraph each check comes from is named against it, so that a
# figure can be traced without reading the whole of Part II.
#
#   phase NAME                       one of: before-start, taxi, take-off,
#                                    climb, cruise, descent, approach,
#                                    landing, after-landing
#   check PROPERTY OP VALUE TEXT...  an item the aircraft can see done
#   range PROPERTY LOW HIGH TEXT...  the same, where a band shows it done
#   confirm TEXT...                  an item only the pilot can see done
#
# with `#` beginning a comment; src/sim/checklist.hpp owns the format.
#
# The Mosquito has no airbrake and no spoiler, so nothing here names one. Its
# radiator shutters are open or shut and nothing between, and its supercharger
# switch is AUTO or MOD, so both are read as over or under half.
#
# **Three things the Notes corrected.** An earlier version of this file was
# written from ordinary practice for the type rather than from the Notes, and
# it had the radiator shutters open for starting where para. 37 has them shut;
# it put the fuel cocks on the main tanks where para. 37 starts on the outer
# ones; and it climbed at 148 knots, the 1944 edition's 170 mph, where the
# 1950 edition's para. 41 gives 150 knots.
#
# **The speed limits below are Part III's**, para. 52 (iv): undercarriage down
# 155 knots, flaps not more than 25 degrees down 175 knots, flaps fully down
# 130 knots. The stalling speeds are para. 43's, and are this project's
# figures in assets/figures/mosquito-fb6.xml.

phase before-start
# Check list items 38 to 51, and para. 37 (i).
confirm Control locks removed and stowed, and the chocks in position
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.2 Throttles half an inch open, item 53 and para. 37
check fcs/advance-cmd-norm >= 0.95 R.p.m. control levers at the maximum r.p.m. position, para. 37
check fcs/mixture-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Mixture up, where the carburettors do the rest
check fcs/supercharger-cmd-norm <= 0.5 Superchargers at MOD, low gear, para. 37
check fcs/cooling-flaps-cmd-norm[0] <= 0.5 Radiator shutters closed for the start, item 66 and para. 37
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps up after the handpump check, item 65
confirm Fuel cocks on the outer tanks and the transfer cock off, para. 37
confirm Harness tight and locked, and the entrance door locked, items 84 and 85

phase taxi
# Check list items 93 and 94, and para. 38: the shutters are opened as part
# of exercising and testing, not before.
check propulsion/engine[0]/engine-rpm >= 600 Port engine running, warmed at 1,200 r.p.m., para. 37
check propulsion/engine[1]/engine-rpm >= 600 Starboard engine running and warming, para. 37
check fcs/cooling-flaps-cmd-norm[0] >= 0.5 Radiator shutters opened at the magneto check, para. 38
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps up
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.4 Taxi on low power, turning on the outer throttle
confirm Chocks clear and the brakes tested as soon as the aircraft moves, items 93 and 94

phase take-off
# Check list items 95 to 105, and para. 40.
range fcs/pitch-trim-cmd-norm -0.35 0.35 Elevator trimmed one to one and a half divisions nose heavy, item 95
check fcs/advance-cmd-norm >= 0.95 R.p.m. control levers at the maximum r.p.m. position, item 97
range fcs/flap-pos-deg 0.0 15.5 Flaps up, or fifteen degrees down, item 99
check fcs/supercharger-cmd-norm <= 0.5 Superchargers at MOD, item 100
check fcs/cooling-flaps-cmd-norm[0] >= 0.5 Radiator shutters open, item 101
check gear/gear-pos-norm >= 0.95 Undercarriage down and locked
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Throttles opened slowly, the swing held on the rudder, para. 40
confirm Taxied forward a few yards to straighten the tailwheel, para. 40

phase climb
# Para. 41 (i) and (ii), and para. 40 (iv) to (vi).
check gear/gear-pos-norm <= 0.05 Undercarriage up once comfortably airborne, para. 40
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps up, the aircraft trimmed slightly tail heavy first, para. 40
range propulsion/engine[0]/engine-rpm 2600 2950 Climbing at 2,850 r.p.m. in low gear, para. 41
range velocities/vc-kts 130 170 Climbing at 150 knots, the speed for the maximum rate, para. 41
check fcs/cooling-flaps-cmd-norm[0] >= 0.5 Radiator shutters open for the climb
check fcs/supercharger-cmd-norm >= 0.5 Superchargers to AUTO as the obtainable boost falls, para. 41
confirm Above 18,000 feet, two knots off the climbing speed for each 1,000 feet, para. 41

phase cruise
# Para. 44.
range propulsion/engine[0]/engine-rpm 2000 2700 The lowest practicable r.p.m., and never above 2,650, paras. 44 and 51
check fcs/cooling-flaps-cmd-norm[0] <= 0.5 Radiator shutters shut: open they cost the aircraft its speed
check fcs/supercharger-cmd-norm <= 0.5 Superchargers at MOD unless 2,650 r.p.m. would be passed, para. 44
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps up
check gear/gear-pos-norm <= 0.05 Undercarriage up
confirm Engines cleared every thirty minutes at 2,850 r.p.m. for thirty seconds, para. 44

phase descent
# Para. 42 (iv), flying at reduced airspeeds.
range fcs/throttle-cmd-norm 0.1 0.6 Throttles back, but kept open enough to keep the engines warm
range propulsion/engine[0]/engine-rpm 2000 2700 R.p.m. controls set to give 2,650, para. 42
check fcs/cooling-flaps-cmd-norm[0] <= 0.5 Radiator shutters shut while the engines are cooling anyway
check fcs/supercharger-cmd-norm >= 0.5 Supercharger left at AUTO on the way down
confirm Speed reduced to 175 knots before the flaps are lowered fifteen degrees, para. 42
confirm Altimeter set to the aerodrome's pressure, item 86

phase approach
# Check list items 106 to 112, in the order the Notes give them.
range velocities/vc-kts 100 160 Speed reduced to 155 knots for the undercarriage, item 110
check gear/gear-pos-norm >= 0.95 Undercarriage down and locked, the green lights on, item 110
range propulsion/engine[0]/engine-rpm 2700 2950 R.p.m. control levers set to give 2,850, item 111
check fcs/supercharger-cmd-norm <= 0.5 Superchargers at MOD, item 109
range fcs/flap-pos-deg 20.0 45.5 Flaps down once below 130 knots, item 112 and para. 52
check fcs/cooling-flaps-cmd-norm[0] >= 0.5 Radiator shutters open for the slow running
confirm Fullest tanks selected, item 108

phase landing
# Item 112's note, and para. 52 (iv) for the speed the flaps may be fully
# down at. The stall with everything down is 95 to 100 knots, para. 43.
check fcs/flap-pos-deg >= 40.0 Flaps fully down, below 130 knots, item 112
check gear/gear-pos-norm >= 0.95 Undercarriage re-selected down with the flaps down, item 112
range velocities/vc-kts 105 130 Over the boundary above the 95 to 100 knot stall, para. 43
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.2 Throttles closed in the hold-off
confirm Wheels first with the tail up, and the brakes only once the speed has gone

phase after-landing
# Check list items 113 to 117, when clear of the landing area.
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps up, selector neutral, item 113
check fcs/cooling-flaps-cmd-norm[0] >= 0.5 Radiator shutters open, item 114
check fcs/advance-cmd-norm >= 0.95 R.p.m. control levers to the maximum r.p.m. position, item 115
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.35 Throttles back to a taxi power
check velocities/vc-kts <= 30 Clear of the landing area and slowed to a taxi
confirm Brake pressure sufficient for taxying, item 117
